{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"de0b621f4348ab2ceeacbfff43022dbcd1da01619e96a9ad66652b8c282a3ad0","digest":{"component_or_area":"reducer cache","key_entities":["src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py","src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py","write_cache","read_cache","process_create","atomic_write","rebar._store.fsutil",".cache.json",".cache.json.tmp","reduce_ticket"],"problem_keywords":["concurrent writers","cache corruption","race condition","stale state","atomic publication","event replay","reducer cache"],"propositions":["Multiple concurrent reducer cache writers use the same fixed .cache.json.tmp temporary file path, causing overlapping file descriptors to the same inode.","After one writer renames .cache.json.tmp into place, another writer can continue mutating the now-visible final cache file, splicing fields from divergent generation envelopes.","A cache publication can carry the current generation hash but stale state fields from a different event generation, causing false cache hits that bypass deterministic replay.","The corrupt-CREATE cache publication in process_create and the normal write_cache function must both route through a canonical atomic_write mechanism with unique temporary files."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786327526169501738,"uuid":"5c4266af-f11e-4440-aab6-8809727cfe15"}